from pathlib import Path
import csv,json,collections
base=Path(__file__).parent;p=base/'release-comparison'
catalog=json.loads((p/'catalog_snapshot.json').read_text())
schema=list(csv.DictReader((p/'database_schema.csv').open(encoding='utf-8')))
mapping=[]
for r in catalog:
    yr=r['release']
    for v in ['GBA6RTT','CTOTALT','UAGRNTN','UAGRNTP','SCUGRAD','ANYAIDP','NPGRN2']:
        matches=[x for x in schema if x['release']==yr and x['column'].upper()==v]
        for x in matches:mapping.append({'release':yr,'variable':v,'actual_table':x['table'],'actual_type':x['type']})
with (p/'tested_measure_locations.csv').open('w',encoding='utf-8-sig',newline='') as f:
    w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=['release','variable','actual_table','actual_type']);w.writeheader();w.writerows(mapping)
lines=['# Annual IPEDS release comparison against 2015–16','','Reviewed October 16, 2026. Baseline means the **2015–16 final collection release**, not two separate baseline files. All ten supplied releases were inspected.','','## Conclusion','','Most survey families are retained, but longitudinal queries need versioned mappings. After removing annual suffixes, all 47 baseline cataloged table families remain represented through 2023–24 (the 2021–22 catalog also contains an unavailable placeholder entry). In 2024–25, 42 baseline families remain and five old family names are replaced in the cost/aid reorganization. This is table-family continuity, not proof that every variable or definition is unchanged.','','The largest documented redesigns occur in 2020–21, 2022–23, and 2024–25. Financial-aid metadata in the supplied 2023–24 workbook also conflicts with the actual database, which would cause queries based only on the workbook to fail.','','## Scope and method','','Read every sheet of every annual Excel codebook, including introductions, metadata definitions, and supplemental new/change sheets where present. Extracted and read all ten Word ReadMes. Opened all ten Access databases read-only with Jackcess; enumerated every user table, source row count, column name, type, width and autonumber status, and read up to three sample records per table.','','This is a comprehensive documentation/schema comparison, not a full statistical validation of every data cell. Database row counts are engine-reported counts; uniqueness, full-column missingness, and numerical distributions have not been profiled across all annual records. No source files were modified.','','Compared each release both to 2015–16 and to its immediate predecessor. Matched annual table families by narrowly normalizing year/period suffixes; preserved variable names and categorical codes. Compared variable labels, long descriptions, type/format, width, multi-record flags and imputation references, plus table descriptions and code labels. Formatting/whitespace and selected year-only differences are distinguished heuristically. Definition candidates still require interpretation: a text diff is not automatically a substantive change. Supplemental source change sheets are retained separately.','','## Annual inventory','','Catalog counts below are unique table identifiers and unique table/variable pairs, not physical Excel used-range row counts. Database table counts include metadata/helper tables.','','| Collection cycle | Release | Database user tables | Cataloged table names | Unique variable entries | Main changes requiring attention |','| --- | --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |']
descriptions=[
'Baseline; five-sheet workbook; core graduation/completions/aid examples verified previously.',
'Pell/subsidized-loan graduation table and derived outcome measures added; finance expense detail removed/reworked; instructional salary measures expanded; explicit variable/value change sheets supplied.',
'Outcome Measures and derived OM variables substantially reorganized; salary variables also change. EFCP detail is not a continuously annual table.',
'EFCP table returns; other variable/code changes are recorded in the register. No wholesale baseline table-family replacement.',
'EFCP not cataloged this cycle; other detailed variable/type/code changes remain. No wholesale baseline table-family replacement.',
'CIP 2020 replaces CIP 2010; certificate levels split; completions distance-education detail expands; 12-month enrollment redesigned; finance/library additions.',
'Parent/child campus characteristics table appears; Carnegie classification fields change; catalog contains EFxxxxCP placeholder absent from database.',
'Aid population splits; gender detail; admissions medians/new considerations; enrollment expansion and terminology updates.',
'High-school credit enrollment table; Pell/loan population detail; workbook aid-table assignments conflict with physical database.',
'New COST1/COST2 organization and unsplit SFA table; classifications change; provisional rather than final.']
for r,d in zip(catalog,descriptions):
    cycle=r['release'].split('_')[1];status=r['release'].rsplit('_',1)[-1]
    lines.append(f"| {cycle} | {status} | {r['database_tables']} | {len(r['tables'])} | {r['variable_entries']:,} | {d} |")
lines+=['','## Confirmed changes and their implications','','### 2016–17: the first baseline transition already changes fields','','The workbook includes `variableChanges1516` and `ValueChanges1516`. Actual common-family schema differences include 62 columns removed from public finance `F1516_F1A`, 58 from private nonprofit finance `F1516_F2`, and 53 from for-profit finance `F1516_F3`, relative to their 2015 counterparts. Many are detailed expense-component fields. These are field removals/reorganizations, not evidence that the corresponding aggregate expense concept disappears.','','`SAL2016_IS` adds 36 columns relative to `SAL2015_IS`, including salary measures equated to a nine-month contract. `GR2016_PELL_SSL` and new derived graduation variables support Pell/subsidized-loan distinctions that are absent from the baseline table set. `DRVOM2016` is added, then its variable scheme changes substantially in 2017–18. Do not reuse one outcome-measure or salary-field map across all years.','','Source evidence: 2016–17 supplemental change sheets, annual variable dictionaries, and physical schemas in `database_schema.csv`.','','### 2020–21: program classifications, enrollment and finance','','The 2020–21 ReadMe explicitly identifies:','','- CIP 2020 replacing CIP 2010 for completions; `C2020_A.CIPCODE` is titled “CIP Code - 2020 Classification.” Earlier releases use CIP 2010. A code string shared across taxonomies is not sufficient evidence of identical program scope. Use a reviewed crosswalk for program-level trends; preserve original classifications.','- The less-than-one-year certificate award level splits into two categories. Broad certificate trends require aggregation rules; the bachelor award level remains available.','- Completions distance-education categories gain detail.','- Twelve-month enrollment gains enrollment/degree-seeking breakdowns and distance-education reporting, including the `EFFY2020_DIST` family. Summing all dimension rows would double-count totals and components.','- Library FTE staffing and finance financial-health, scholarship/allowance, and endowment measures expand. Availability begins with the applicable release; earlier absence is not zero.','','### 2021–22: campus detail and classification versions','','`IC2021_PCCAMPUSES` appears. Campus-level reporting must not be joined to institution-level totals without explicit cardinality/reporting rules. Carnegie fields change versions over the period; later classifications cannot be applied to earlier years as though they were recorded then.','','The catalog lists `EFxxxxCP` (Tables21 row 19), but no such physical table exists in the supplied database. Do not fabricate an annual filename or infer an available data series from this placeholder.','','### 2022–23: populations and categories expand','','The ReadMe explicitly documents degree/certificate-seeking versus non-degree/non-certificate-seeking aid detail; graduate enrollment by full-/part-time status; admissions 50th-percentile scores and additional considerations; and gender data for students not categorized into men/women in several components. The source terminology changes from “Nonresident alien” to “U.S. Nonresident.”','','The importer must preserve new dimension codes and totals. Do not assume men + women equals the overall total in every later table. Distinguish a wording update from a population change by consulting each definition. The added GR gender table is not a substitute for the historic bachelor completion-rate series.','','### 2023–24: high-school enrollment and an important metadata conflict','','The ReadMe identifies credit enrollment of high-school students by race/ethnicity and gender; `EFFY2023_HS` is new relative to the preceding catalog. Pell/federal-loan aid gains degree-seeking/non-degree-seeking detail.','','**High severity for automated querying: the supplied workbook assigns many aid fields to the opposite SFA part from the actual Access schema.** For example:','','| Variable | 2023–24 workbook assignment | Actual Access table |','| --- | --- | --- |','| `UAGRNTP` | `SFA2223_P2` (varTable23 row 1497) | `sfa2223_p1` |','| `ANYAIDP` | `SFA2223_P2` (row 1533) | `sfa2223_p1` |','| `NPGRN2` | `SFA2223_P1` (row 1455) | `sfa2223_p2` |','','There are 344 documented variable placements absent from their named physical tables in this release: 246 on P1 and 98 on P2. The three examples above are verified placement conflicts; do not automatically swap every field without checking. Keep original documentation intact, and add reviewed physical-location overrides with provenance. Table-name capitalization itself is not the issue; matching was case-insensitive.','','Two additional documented fields in 2022–23, `SFA2122_P1.SCFA2ND` and `PCCAMPUS`, are absent from the supplied physical table. Their availability must remain unresolved until mapped or confirmed unavailable.','','### 2024–25: COST reorganization','','The ReadMe explicitly says tuition/cost-of-attendance fields move from Institutional Characteristics into COST1, while average net price and the aid information used in its calculation move from SFA into COST2. Physical tables confirm the new organization:','','| Earlier family | Latest organization | Implication |','| --- | --- | --- |','| `ICyyyy_AY`, `ICyyyy_PY` and some IC fields | `Cost1_2024` | Map by definitions and calendar/program coverage; not merely a table rename. |','| `DRVICyyyy` cost indicators | `DRVCOST2024` | Derived cost measures need updated locations. |','| SFA net-price measures | `COST2_2024_NetPrice` | `NPGRN2` is physically here. |','| Aid information supporting net-price calculations | `Cost2_2024_FinancialAid` | Preserve its first-time/full-time populations and multiyear reference periods. |','| General student aid formerly on SFA part tables | `SFA2324` | `UAGRNTP`, `UAGRNTN`, `SCUGRAD`, `ANYAIDP` are physically available here. |','','The old IC_AY/IC_PY/DRVIC and SFA_P1/SFA_P2 family names are absent from the latest table catalog. This is a confirmed organizational change, not evidence that all their measures were discontinued. The latest data are provisional and must be labeled and versioned accordingly.','','## Implications for our tested measures','','| Concept | Observed structural continuity | Remaining validation |','| --- | --- | --- |','| Six-year bachelor completion | `DRVGR2015` through `DRVGR2024` all physically contain `GBA6RTT`; source integer type is stable. | Verify each annual cohort/outcome date and underlying count/filter definitions before certifying a trend. Baseline description contains stale cohort references. |','| Bachelor degrees awarded | `C2015_A` through `C2024_A` contain `CTOTALT`, `MAJORNUM`, and `AWLEVEL` with stable physical types. | Keep first-major/total-row rules, and use CIP-version crosswalks for program breakdowns. |','| All-undergraduate grant aid | `UAGRNTP`, `UAGRNTN`, and `SCUGRAD` exist in each annual physical database. | Correct 2023 workbook placement; map to `SFA2324` for the latest release; verify annual population/time definitions. |','| Any aid for entering students | `ANYAIDP` exists across releases. | It remains distinct from all-undergraduate grant aid; do not combine populations. |','| Net price | `NPGRN2` exists across the physical releases inspected. | Correct 2023 metadata location and map to COST2 in 2024; rolling suffixes reference different periods each release. |','','See `tested_measure_locations.csv` for exact physical tables and types by release. Presence and stable type do not alone certify longitudinal comparability.','','## Metadata/database reconciliation','','Across the ten releases, the automated placement checks found 1,248 records requiring classification: 346 documented fields absent from their named physical table, one documented table absent, and 901 physical columns missing from the variable dictionary for cataloged tables. Of the latter, 505 are UNITID entries; shared identifiers being omitted from a dictionary is not equivalent to corrupt data. Other entries include helper/revision fields. Do not interpret this total as 1,248 independent substantive errors.','','The mismatch register preserves the evidence instead of silently repairing sources. The financial-aid placement conflicts, absent fields, and EFxxxxCP placeholder above are the highest-priority confirmed issues. Workbook used ranges sometimes include blank or duplicate documentation rows; parsers must use content and keys rather than max_row as an entry count.','','Code frequencies/percentages naturally vary with annual data and were not treated as definition changes. Added/removed code entries can also reflect which categories occur in the release; not every such diff is a taxonomy redesign. Annual changes in row counts or sample values are not interpreted as quality failures.','','## Changes needed in the architecture/importer','','1. Use a per-release physical schema registry and codebook catalog; table-name templating alone is insufficient.','2. Keep original metadata and separately record reviewed corrections. Resolve documented-to-physical placement before executing a plan.','3. Store definition/taxonomy/population versions and annual period interpretation, especially CIP 2010/2020, cost/aid moves, classification versions and expanded enrollment/gender categories.','4. Preserve all supplementary change sheets, even when absent in adjacent releases or differently named.','5. Fail visibly on absent fields, unknown types and ambiguous table mappings. Do not silently fill missing annual measures with zero.','6. Validate record grain and reporting-unit joins before importing harmonized views. Raw records remain faithful to their annual sources.','7. Build reviewed mappings for graduation, awards and grant aid first, followed by the wider discovery catalog. Every new concept still needs a supported plan.','','## Evidence and reproducibility','','- `database_schema.csv`: every physical user-table column, source row count and type.','- `database_samples.csv`: up to three sampled records per table, for structural inspection only.','- `sheet_inventory.csv`: every workbook tab and used range.','- `catalog_snapshot.json`: annual table descriptions, periods and catalog counts.','- `change_register.csv`: exhaustive automated baseline and predecessor differences, with old/new text and source row locations. This is a review queue, not a certified semantic crosswalk.','- `metadata_database_mismatches.csv`: documented/physical discrepancies.','- `tested_measure_locations.csv`: physical locations of our tested measures.','- Annual extracted ReadMe and supplementary worksheet files: release-specific evidence.','- `../compare_releases.py`, `../InspectRelease.java`: extraction/comparison implementation.','- `comparison_review.ipynb`: runnable review of the saved evidence.','','Original sources are under the user-designated `IPEDS Data` folder. Database schemas came from those Access files; codebook evidence came from their paired workbooks. ReadMe descriptions are reported as source claims, not blindly accepted when they conflict with physical files (for example, file-format/date wording in release notes).','','## Completion and limits','','Completed: all ten releases opened; all codebook sheets and ReadMes extracted/read; all user-table schemas and row counts compared; sample records inspected; structural and documented changes registered; major longitudinal risks interpreted.','','Not yet completed: full annual data import, every-record data-quality profiling, independent validation of every changed definition, exact source hashes, every semantic crosswalk, and certification of longitudinal numerical results. These belong to the next ingestion/mapping stages.']
(base/'RELEASE_COMPARISON.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
nb={'nbformat':4,'nbformat_minor':5,'metadata':{'kernelspec':{'display_name':'Python 3','language':'python','name':'python3'}},'cells':[
 {'cell_type':'markdown','metadata':{},'source':['# Review annual IPEDS schema evidence\n','Reads saved source inspections. Run InspectRelease.java and compare_releases.py from the parent folder to regenerate evidence. The extraction is structural and samples up to three records per physical table; it is not a full numerical data audit.']},
 {'cell_type':'code','execution_count':None,'metadata':{},'outputs':[],'source':['from pathlib import Path\nimport json, csv, collections\np = Path.cwd()\nif not (p / "catalog_snapshot.json").exists():\n    p = p / "agent-redesign" / "release-comparison"\ncatalog = json.loads((p / "catalog_snapshot.json").read_text())\n[(r["release"], r["database_tables"], len(r["tables"]), r["variable_entries"]) for r in catalog]']},
 {'cell_type':'code','execution_count':None,'metadata':{},'outputs':[],'source':['with (p / "metadata_database_mismatches.csv").open(encoding="utf-8-sig") as f:\n    mismatches = list(csv.DictReader(f))\ncollections.Counter(r["issue"] for r in mismatches)']},
 {'cell_type':'code','execution_count':None,'metadata':{},'outputs':[],'source':['with (p / "tested_measure_locations.csv").open(encoding="utf-8-sig") as f:\n    locations = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n[r for r in locations if r["variable"] in ("UAGRNTP", "NPGRN2")]']}
]}
(p/'comparison_review.ipynb').write_text(json.dumps(nb,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('Report and review notebook written')
